### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?

Item 3 of #13036 suggests that [prepare content patching](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#prepare-content-patching) increment *scope*'s node document's [throw-on-dynamic-markup-insertion counter](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dynamic-markup-insertion.html#throw-on-dynamic-markup-insertion-counter) around its removal loop. WebKit's implementation (https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/76083) now does that, and so does Chromium (`NodeRemovalScope` in `patch.cc`).

However, *scope* doesn't have to be in the document whose parser is running. Script can move a patch's insertion target into another document mid-patch; `template-for-move-cross-document.html` tests exactly that. The scope of a `<template for>` nested in that patch is then in the other document:

```js
// iframe is a same-origin <iframe> in document.
const doc = iframe.contentDocument;
doc.open();
doc.write(`<div id="target"><?start name="outer">old<?end></div>`);
doc.write(`<template for="outer"><?start name="inner"><iframe></iframe><?end>`);
document.body.append(doc.getElementById("target"));
document.querySelector("#target iframe").contentWindow.onpagehide = () => doc.write("<p>Hi");
doc.write(`<template for="inner">New</template></template>`);
```

Removing the inner range fires `pagehide`. The counter has been incremented on the outer `document`, not on `doc`, so `doc.write()` goes ahead. It re-enters `doc`'s tokenizer while tree construction is still processing the inner template's start tag. With the WebKit PR applied, a Debug build hits the tree builder's re-entrancy assertion here.

[Create an element for a token](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#create-an-element-for-the-token) has the same shape. It increments the counter of *targetParent*'s node document. For a patch, *targetParent* is the insertion target, and script can move that to another document too. WebKit increments the counter of the document being parsed in that case.

The counter on *scope*'s node document is still needed. For a streaming fragment parser, that is the document `template-for-pagehide-dynamic-markup-insertion.html` expects to throw. So I suggest also incrementing the counter of the parser's `Document`, in both algorithms, whenever it differs from the node document used today.
